title: Install Tearoff Panes

\rules except wikilink

! Tearoff Panes

Open any tiddler in a draggable, resizable pane that floats over the main story river, without leaving the current browser window or document.

Drag the button below onto an ''already-open'' TiddlyWiki document in another tab or window to install it there -- no download needed.

<$button dragTiddler="$:/plugins/phriendly/tearoff-panes" class="tc-btn-big-green">
{{$:/core/images/download-button}} Drag me into your own TiddlyWiki
</$button>

!! Making the drag work

A drag like this only carries the plugin data between tabs of the ''same''
browser -- it can't cross from this page into a different browser (for
example, this page open in Chrome and your wiki open in Firefox). Dragging
straight from one tab to another also isn't always obvious, since the two
tabs usually aren't visible at the same time. Get both tabs on screen at
once first, in whichever way your browser supports:

* Drag this tab out of its tab bar to pop it into its own window, then drag the button across into your wiki's window.
* Or right-click this tab and look for an option like //Move tab to new window//.
* Or, if your browser offers a split-view / side-by-side tabs feature (recent Edge, Firefox, and others do), use that to show both tabs at once without needing separate windows.

Can't get that working, or your wiki is open in a different browser?
Download
[[tearoff-panes-0.0.4.html|https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mMerlin/tw5-tearoff-panes/v0.0.4/dist/tearoff-panes-0.0.4.html]]
instead, then drag //that file// into your wiki, or use Tools &rarr; import.
This always works, regardless of browser.

See the [[GitHub repository|https://github.com/mMerlin/tw5-tearoff-panes]] for documentation, source, and version history.
